#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# between

#% text
# `between(x, [a, b])` is `a <= x and x <= b`; `between(x, [[a1, b1], [a2, b2], ...])` holds when x is in one of the ranges.

#% text
# `between([a, b])` is the operator form: `between([a, b])(x)` is `between(x, [a, b])`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A range may also be an `interval(...)` or a `centered_interval(c, w)` (the range `[c - w, c + w]`).

#% item
# When x is an interval it must lie inside one of the ranges.

#% item
# Numerical comparisons are decided; symbolic ones stay as inequalities.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
between(3, [2, 5])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
between(x, [a, b])
#% output
#= a <= x and x <= b

#% cell
select([5, 10, 15, 20, 25], between([10, 20]))
#% output
#= [10, 15, 20]

#% cell
between(2, [e, pi])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
between(interval([3, 4]), centered_interval(5, 3))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
between(6, [[2, 5], [8, 12]])
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `interval`, `clip`, `rescale`
